{"author":{"id":"a51b5961cc6de343a64125d8eb6a0f965aa434020b9c46ed932a1bbf143eb532"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791594541,"nonce":"tAgr/HKzJuBllb1xiK+e36V845A=","message":"Paint is now read in Rust (2026-10-10). The TypeScript host parsed nine paint properties from resolved strings and dropped the rest silently; one engine now reads every paint declaration, the way layout declarations are read. This is the step the earlier note left open: \"routing paint natively is the next step\".\n\nWhere: blinc_abi css/paint.rs (paint_writes, the counterpart of layout_writes), with color, gradient, transform, filter, shadow, border and quantity beside it, on branch css-paint in /Users/amaterasu/Vibranium/blinc_abi-paint, not landed (see the issue titled \"Land the blinc_abi css-paint branch\"). The parsers return typed values, the cascade hands them to the host as writes, and the addon applies them to the scene (native/src/scene.rs apply_paint). Paint output is opt-in per Styles, so a host that draws from resolved declarations is untouched.\n\nWhat reads now that did not: hsl(), color-mix(), currentcolor and the full named colours; linear and radial gradients; background: glass with glass-*; transform; filter; mask-image; border and the per-side shorthands with per-side colours, border-style, thin/medium/thick; outline. A value it cannot read is reported with its reason and the rest of its rule still applies.\n\nAlso fixed: Host.createElement did not describe a plain element to the cascade, so type, universal and structural selectors never matched it. And a new optional module, blinc_ts/theme/user-agent, gives built-in elements theme-driven defaults.\n\nRewritten, not patched: the TypeScript paint parsers and parseColor are gone from the host (only a Brush or colour array set directly stays in TypeScript, over the cascade, until cleared).\n\nVerified: blinc_abi css tests 57 (parsers, error text, restyle with unsets, currentcolor following the node's colour, borders giving layout space), scene suite 85, default-features build; blinc_ts native-css-paint renders gradients, colours, transform, filter, mask, glass, borders and outlines and checks pixels and layout. Each parser's tests were checked by mutating the parser and seeing them fail.\n\nLeft: clip-path, overflow-fade, backdrop-filter, url() backgrounds, text-decoration and text-align, in their own issue; transition and animation stay in 35f7bd0.","files":null}]}